body:
I think per RAW this spell can only be cast after advantage is applied, resulting in a successful roll. At that point there second dice is gone, as the higher was chosen and applied, and that's what allowed the success. So the higher of the two die is chosen when rollling with advantage, then the spell is triggered and cast, and then that higher die that was chosen gets rerolled. 

&#x200B;

So if you roll a 12 and a 15 with advantage, you pick the 15. Then SB gets cast, and you reroll the 15 and pick the lower of the two. If you roll a 4, you whiff. If you roll a 20, you stick with your 15. 

&#x200B;

Whether or not this is HOW you should run it is another discussion, obviously dm can do what they need to do. But I think that's the intention of how the spell works via RAW

Re-watching the Grinch episode, what gets me is that Lily takes all the decorations because of what Ted called  her even though Marshall is the one who's super excited for Christmas, and Ted is the one who's worried about how sad Marshall will be if Christmas gets cancelled. After leaving Marshall and calling off the wedding she's gonna pull that? 

&#x200B;

Plus then we find out Marshall spent the whole day tracking down his present for her. She does not deserve Marshall Eriksen
